<title>USA: BPA OFFERS 200 MW PEAK MONDAY POWER AT $21-23/MWH.</title>
<headline>BPA OFFERS 200 MW PEAK MONDAY POWER AT $21-23/MWH.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) offered 200 megawatts of peak, firm power for Tuesday delivery, the agency said Monday.</p>
<p>The Portland, Oregon-based federal power marketing agency offered Northwest sales at $21.00 per megawatt hour (MWh) and California-Oregon border deliveries at $23.00.</p>
<p>For Monday, BPA had offered 400 MW of peak firm electricity at $18.00 a MWh for Northwest sales and $20.00 for California-Oregon border deliveries.</p>
<p>Monday offers also included non-firm power during peak and off-peak hours.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 213 955 6761))</p>
</text>
